#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:42
msgid "GitHub releases and webhooks"
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:52
msgid "Use GitHub releases for an eligible plugin or theme only after you have reviewed the exact uploaded release ZIP. Booster checks the selected release again before WordPress changes files."
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:53
msgid "Publish a GitHub release"
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:55
msgid "Upload one eligible installable plugin or theme ZIP as the release asset. Do not use GitHub’s generated source archive."
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:56
msgid "Keep the release tag and the canonical WordPress Version header aligned. Keep the package Update URI aligned with the selected GitHub repository. Plugins need one eligible top-level plugin header; themes need root style.css. A mismatch is rejected."
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:57
msgid "GitHub immutable releases are optional supply-chain hardening. Booster does not enable that repository setting through its setup pull request."
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:59
msgid "About GitHub releases"
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:59
msgid " (opens in a new tab)"
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:59
msgid "About immutable releases"
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:60
msgid "Use the setup pull request deliberately"
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:61
msgid "Review the generated setup pull request in the repository. It prepares release workflow files; it does not publish a release, merge changes, enable immutable releases, or replace your repository review policy."
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:62
msgid "Check deliveries and remove retired hooks"
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:63
msgid "GitHub does not automatically redeliver failed deliveries. Test a delivery from GitHub, then compare its delivery identifier with the Provider request ID in Booster Activity. A missing Activity entry is inconclusive for probes, ignored events, and zero-target deliveries."
msgstr ""

#: src/GitHubDocumentation.php:64
msgid "For a known GitHub hook, use Booster’s verified Remove action before removing a local signing secret. That action removes the remote hook and releases only a repository secret created specifically for it. Confirm that no branch-managed package still needs the repository hook or an owner-shared secret. If ownership or remaining use is uncertain, leave the setup in place."
msgstr ""
